1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,500
One drawing. Two counts.
Which one do you price?

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,700
Before a builder can price a job,

3
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,500
someone has to turn drawings
into quantities.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,500
When two readings disagree,
the work starts all over again.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,500
Which symbols were counted,
and where are they on the plan?

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,500
On this test drawing, one detector
proposed three candidates.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,500
The other proposed ten.

8
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,000
None of their proposals matched.

9
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,700
The team needed to see where
the disagreement came from.

10
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:38,500
Upload a drawing
and ask Sona a question.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
PlanProof can use geometry rules and
machine learning to find evidence.

12
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,500
When needed, NVIDIA Nemotron
can inspect a specific crop.

13
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,500
Gemini writes Sona's final response.

14
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:13,500
Click a citation and the workspace
takes you to the exact area on the drawing.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
If the evidence is inconclusive, Sona
tells you what still needs checking.

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Find the quantity.

17
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:44,500
Follow the evidence.

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Try PlanProof.
